WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.980
<i>When I was in middle school,</i>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.480
<i>I would have never guessed that 
I'd be climbing mountains.</i>

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.860
<i>Yet, here I am now.</i>

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.570
<i>I walked all the way here on my own.</i>

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.390
<i>I'm tired, yet I can't sleep.</i>

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:20.450
<i>But it's unlike that one night 
I spent in a mountain shed.</i>

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.640
<i>I wonder what scenery I'll see tomorrow.</i>

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:27.440
<i>My mind's abuzz with excitement, 
and I can't sleep.</i>

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.140
Aoi-chan.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.760
Aoi-san.

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:32.230
Could you come outside for a second?

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.100
The sky cleared up.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.620
It looks like it'll be nice tomorrow, too.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:51.550
<i>Kaede Saito-san.</i>

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.150
<i>She's one year ahead of me at my high school.</i>

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.110
<i>She's my senpai in mountain climbing, too.</i>

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:00.520
The fox, the dolphin, the foal...

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.740
I can't believe they're so visible.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:04.330
<i>Kokona Aoba-chan.</i>

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.120
<i>She's knowledgeable and ladylike.</i>

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.630
<i>She's a dependable middle schooler.</i>

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.000
<i>They're both my precious friends.</i>

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.290
<i>My mountain buddies.</i>

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:18.640
<i>But the reason I started mountain climbing...</i>

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:21.920
<i>The first person to invite 
me to the mountains...</i>

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:23.390
<i>was her.</i>

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.090
<i>Hinata Kuraue.</i>

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:34.460
<i>It all started when I ran into Hinata again.</i>

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:10.200
<b>Wareiwa Bridge</b>

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:10.200
<b>"First Date at Mt. Tsukuba!?"</b>

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.460
<i>Summer break felt so short.</i>

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.450
<b>September 1st</b>

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.450
<b>Shimada  Furuhashi</b>

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.500
Mt. Tanigawa

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:23.020
<i>Oh, yeah... I haven't given 
Hinata anything to thank her</i>

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:26.010
<i>for the gift she gave me at Mt. Fuji.</i>

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.660
Morning!

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.520
How was summer break?

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.660
I mean, we saw each other almost every day.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.120
Morning.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:35.020
Morning.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.670
Morning!

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:38.650
M-Morning...

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:42.910
It's a new term...

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:48.010
I saw the night scenery from the Sky Deck 
at Sunshine as a memory of summer.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:49.390
It was amazing.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.160
Yeah, it was like a chest full of jewels.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.100
It was so windy.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.690
Lucky!

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:58.150
Have you <i>seen</i> the <i>scene</i>ry?

00:03:58.610 --> 00:03:59.520
Get it?

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.920
What the heck?

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.930
Have you never seen the night 
scenery from anywhere, Hinata-chan?

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.930
I guess I've seen some during the 
fireworks festival at Tenran Hill.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:10.930
<i>Night scenery, huh?</i>

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.980
<i>I wonder if I can combine mountain climbing 
and night scenery for my gift to Hinata.</i>

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:18.730
Hanasaika Susuki

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:22.240
Hikari-san, do you know of a place on top 
of a mountain with nice scenery at night?

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.110
Did you finally find a boyfriend, Aoi-chan?!

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.870
Oh, no! We have to let Mom know!

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.820
No, I'm going with Hinata!

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.030
Oh.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:33.870
Sure. Right.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:37.100
The view's really pretty 
at night from Mt. Tsukuba.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:41.030
You can get pretty high up by car, 
and you take a ropeway to the top.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:43.380
You can see all of Tokyo!

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:45.090
Even though it's in Ibaraki!

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:49.100
<i>Hikari-san knows a lot, surprisingly.</i>

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.950
<i>I wonder if we could walk up Mt. Tsukuba.</i>

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:55.390
<i>I could surprise her with the scenery, and...</i>

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.900
Come on, it's so boring 
walking here at night.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.920
Whoa, what the heck? That's crazy!

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:03.910
<i>That's it!</i>

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.270
Thank you!

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:07.160
I'll think about Mt. Tsukuba.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.580
Good luck on your first date.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.440
Aoi-chan!

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:14.080
Please keep your relationship 
appropriate for a high schooler.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.830
<b>Hanasaika Susuki</b>

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.830
I told you, that's not what it is!

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.060
Mt. Tsukuba...

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.980
877 meters above sea level.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:26.840
It's not that high, but it's one of 
the top 100 mountains in Japan, huh?

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:31.640
It'll be hard to get to and from Hanno, 
but there's a shuttle bus from the station.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.960
If we take the ropeway back 
at around this time...

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.080
Mom would just barely be okay with it.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:43.860
Hey, Hinata, about the break after next...

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:52.490
The sun's setting.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:54.110
Are we really climbing now?

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:57.220
I wanted to change things up a little.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:00.000
You brought a headlamp 
like I told you to, right?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:01.010
Yeah.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.050
<b>Mt. Nyotai Peak 1.8km</b>

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.050
<b>Mt. Tsukuba Shrine 2.1km</b>

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:04.450
Look, it's called Mt. Nyotai.

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:07.450
Maybe it'll give you a nice 
figure when you climb it.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:09.550
I doubt that'll happen.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.270
There are toads everywhere.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:17.860
Toad oil is a local specialty 
here, apparently.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:18.810
Why?

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.900
It's supposed to be good for your skin.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:24.150
<b>Free Jumbo Slide</b>

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.230
A jumbo slide!

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.150
And it's free!

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.700
What are you, a kid?

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:31.820
Hello.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.030
Hello.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.910
It's well-maintained and easy to walk on.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:38.330
This is just the beginning.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:41.070
<i>Walking like this, just the two of us,</i>

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:44.340
<i>reminds me of the time we first 
climbed Mt. Tenran together.</i>

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:52.880
<i>Even those sloped trails 
were pretty tough back then.</i>

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:57.460
<b>Mt. Nyotai Peak 0.8km</b>

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:57.460
<b>Tsutsujigaoka Descent 1km</b>

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:00.240
We're out in the open.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:02.730
They said it's the remnants 
of Benkei Tea House.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.990
Benkei had tea here?

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:09.010
No, there used to be a tea house 
here named Benkei Tea House.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:10.740
Let's take a little break.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.490
Mt. Nyotai Main Hall

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.490
Mt. Nyotai

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:14.490
It was like hiking up until now,

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:17.720
but there's supposed to be a 
challenging rocky stretch called

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:20.300
the Shirakumobashi Course up ahead.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:21.370
Be ready.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:25.020
You couldn't even find these trails 
if you didn't have a light.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.070
Why are we going up at this hour?

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:30.750
You'll see when we get there.

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:37.430
"Benkei Nanamodori"?

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.190
Benkei again.

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:40.480
Are we going through here?

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:44.990
Whoa, crazy!

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:48.480
It's a miracle that it's never 
collapsed during an earthquake.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.240
<b>Mother's Womb
Pass</b>

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.240
"Pass through the rocks,

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:57.150
and you'll be reborn."

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:58.360
Where?

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:00.250
It's too dark. I can't see.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:02.680
In'yoseki.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:05.270
It's too dark to see this one, too.

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:05.960
Aoi...

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:08.340
Boo!

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:09.610
What are you doing?

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:10.270
Er...

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.010
<b>Mt. Nyotai
Peak 750m</b>

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:18.970
All these rocks are amazing.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:19.380
<b>Rimen
Daikoku</b>

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.140
Mt. Fuji was amazing, too,

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:21.140
<b>National
Treasure</b>

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:25.400
but it's even more thrilling here, 
since there's no one else around.

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:27.400
I think I like this kind of thing.

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:28.650
Really?

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:30.650
I'm glad, then.

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:35.240
<i>Mt. Fuji was like this, too.</i>

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.650
<i>But I'm okay now.</i>

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:44.000
<i>Maybe I've grown since then.</i>

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.840
<i>I wonder if I could make it up Mt. Fuji now.</i>

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.170
<b>Mt. Nyotai Peak</b>

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:55.270
Huh?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.870
Is this the peak?

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:58.680
No way!

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:01.640
<i>There's no view here!</i>

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:05.560
You can get up this way.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.060
<b>Top 100 Japanese Mountains
Mt. Tsukuba</b>

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:22.180
This is awesome, Aoi!

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:37.600
It's more than I expected.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:41.220
I heard this is called night hiking.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:45.010
This comes really late, but remember 
that Mt. Fuji doll you got me?

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:46.190
This is in return for that.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.190
How is it?

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:49.740
Aoi...

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:52.530
It's gorgeous here!

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:54.440
I'm so glad I came! Thanks!

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:58.200
You're welcome.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:09.230
I could look at this forever.

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:11.250
I don't want to move for a while.

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:15.440
Don't forget we have to 
catch the bus back to home.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.540
Yeah.

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:20.110
Hey, Hinata...

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:21.250
Yeah?

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:24.930
What was it like at the top of Mt. Fuji?

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.650
It was pretty.

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:29.480
There's nothing above the ground.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:33.030
It was like I was taking a walk in the sky.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.250
I wish you could have seen it.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:40.800
Yeah?

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:46.110
I was thinking as I was walking today...

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:50.860
I want to get in better shape 
next time, and learn more,

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:54.440
and take on Mt. Fuji again.

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:56.580
Do you think I can?

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:58.930
Let's give it a shot, then!

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:00.260
I'm rooting for you!

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.140
Thanks.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:06.800
If you don't make it again, 
we can think about that then.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:10.020
I'll do my best.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:11.150
Yeah.

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:17.160
We're taking the ropeway down.

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:17.900
Okay.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.780
<i>Hikari-san really helped me out this time.</i>

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:25.420
<i>I wonder how she knew about
a place like this, though.</i>

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:31.720
Couples everywhere.

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:34.180
Hikari-san must have come with her boyfriend.

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:35.130
V!

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:38.310
We're kind of like a couple, too.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:40.320
We're leaving!

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:42.630
Come on, let's check it out for a bit.

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:44.150
The lights are so pretty.

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.010
No way!

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:52.480
<i>That really kills my determination.</i>

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:56.830
<i>My second Mt. Fuji attempt 
is off to a rocky start.</i>

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.990
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.210
<i>To be continued.</i>
